  "M200_1e14": 0.0,
  "notes": "The Local Void (Tully et al. 2008, ApJ 676, 184) — the nearest major cosmic void, spanning ~45 Mpc radius adjacent to our Local Group. Centred at SGX≈−3, SGY≈11 Mpc in supergalactic coordinates, it contributes ~260 km/s to the Milky Way peculiar velocity. Interior galaxy density is <20% of mean cosmic density. Population dominated by blue, star-forming dwarf irregulars (Kreckel et al. 2012, AJ 144, 16) with elevated HI mass fractions and suppressed AGN activity. The void wall harbours IC 342, NGC 6946 (Fireworks Galaxy), and NGC 6503 — prime settlement-zone anchor galaxies. No hot ICM (tx_kev=0); no ram-pressure stripping; pristine ISM conditions throughout. Far-wall galaxies (~63-68 Mpc from us) are SDSS-detected faint irregulars on the Sculptor supercluster boundary. All system_architecture fields reflect void ecology: low ICM stress, reduced metallicity, elevated gas fractions, and minimal AGN feedback. Exoloc addresses use scope void-world (e.g. exotopia:void-world:Local-Void/NGC6503).",
